      "widgets_values": [
        "For the target video, at 0.00 seconds into the target video, <Picture 1> (from [Shot 1]) is fully referenced.\n\nintegrated_multimodal_description:\n\n[Shot 1]\nThe spacecraft shown in Picture 1 rapidly launches upward through the atmosphere. The camera follows the spacecraft from below in a dynamic low-angle tracking shot as powerful engine flames burn beneath it. Thick clouds rush downward and become increasingly distant as the spacecraft climbs higher. The spacecraft remains clearly visible and consistent with Picture 1, with realistic acceleration and strong atmospheric motion.\n\n[Shot 2] at 00:02:300\nHard cut to a closer exterior view of the same ascending spacecraft. The camera rapidly pushes forward toward the cockpit with a smooth, controlled zoom-in while the spacecraft continues flying upward. The cockpit window becomes increasingly prominent in frame. Reflections of the bright sky move naturally across the glass, and the astronaut's silhouette gradually becomes visible inside.\n\n[Shot 3] at 00:04:200\nHard cut to the interior cockpit. A young woman astronaut in a realistic white spacesuit is seated and securely strapped into the pilot's seat. The camera makes a subtle slow push-in toward her face while the spacecraft continues accelerating. She looks forward at the controls, then briefly looks toward the camera and says clearly in a calm but excited voice: \"We're entering space.\"\n\nShe turns her attention back toward the windshield as the cockpit vibrates subtly from the spacecraft's acceleration.\n\nOverall soundscape: powerful rocket-engine roar during the first two shots, rushing atmospheric wind and structural vibration during ascent, transitioning to a muffled engine sound inside the cockpit with subtle electronic instrument beeps and the astronaut's breathing.\n\nNon-diegetic music: restrained cinematic tension building during the launch and cockpit approach, then resolving into a sense of awe as the astronaut says, \"We're entering space.\"\n",
        1344,
        768,
        124
      ]
